From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giga Edge SDK <noreply@giga-edge-sdk.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:31:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] llama: fused MTP drafts in llama_decode

The MTP (NextN) blocks of Qwen3 run in the same llama_decode as the main
model: llama_set_mtp_fused, llama_get_mtp_fused, llama_get_mtp_drafts_ith and
LLAMA_HAS_MTP_FUSED. Drafts come from the last output of the ubatch or, in a
verification batch, from the first row whose argmax differs from the next
token. The verification batch uses the split_rows mode of flash attention, so
its rows match step-by-step generation bitwise.

The MTP blocks apply rope_freqs like the main layers. test-mtp-rope-factors
checks that a model with rope_freqs 2.0 gives the same logits and drafts bit
for bit as the same model without the tensor run with freq_scale 0.5.
